      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's about twice the maximum recommended daily dose:\n\n- **Immediate-release:** the maximum is 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily.\n- **Extended-release:** the maximum is 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day.\n\nA dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **850 mg** by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg/day** in total, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** per dose, or some other regimen\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is deliberate, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose. Pharmacy may still flag it."
      }
     ],
